From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:54:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: refuse HEVC 4:4:4

An HEVC 4:4:4 frame (chroma_format_idc 3, at 8 or 10 bits) is never
completed. It times out, and the recovery resets the whole decoder,
failing every other stream's frames too. The driver has no 4:4:4
capture format either: such a stream was set up with a 4:2:0 picture
buffer.

Refuse it when the SPS is set, next to the existing refusals of 12-bit
and 4:2:2 10-bit. 4:0:0 and 4:2:2 8-bit streams decode bit-exact and
are still accepted.

Signed-off-by: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
(cherry picked from commit ba647ce960996682b8c151d684dc11cadab464c4)
[dylan: one co-author trailer of the original message is not reproduced here]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c
index db894214c4..accabe2c64 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c
@@ -1088,11 +1088,7 @@ static enum avd_image_fmt avd_hevc_get_image_fmt(struct avd_ctx *ctx,
 	if (ctrl->id != V4L2_CID_STATELESS_HEVC_SPS)
 		return AVD_IMG_FMT_ANY;
 
-	/*
-	 * TODO: we can do up to 4:4:4 12 bit
-	 * not sure if v4l2 supports RExt
-	 */
-
+	/* avd_hevc_validate_sps() refuses 4:4:4 and depths other than 8/10. */
 	if (sps->bit_depth_luma_minus8 == 0) {
 		if (sps->chroma_format_idc == 2)
 			return AVD_IMG_FMT_422_8BIT;
@@ -1127,6 +1123,13 @@ static int avd_hevc_validate_sps(struct avd_ctx *ctx,
 	if (sps->chroma_format_idc == 2 && sps->bit_depth_luma_minus8 == 2)
 		/* 4:2:2 10 bit would need P210, which is not offered */
 		return -EINVAL;
+	if (sps->chroma_format_idc > 2)
+		/*
+		 * 4:4:4 has no capture format, and its frames are never
+		 * completed: each times out and resets the whole decoder.
+		 * 4:0:0, 4:2:0 and 4:2:2 at 8 bits decode.
+		 */
+		return -EINVAL;
 
 	return 0;
 }
